💭 As reraiseInitializerArgument, but the receiver's class stores its generic arguments, and the initializer is
💭 called with a local generic argument of the calling generic method. The generic argument descriptions it is
💭 passed are then allocated dynamically, rather than being a compile-time constant, and must be freed if evaluating
💭 an argument to the initializer reraises before the initializer, which is what would make it own them, is entered.
